Their order sizes are close to the target for the cost structure, with a small buffer above mean demand:\n- Product 0 covers 3 days of demand, about 42 on average. Its 4-day shelf life means leftovers rarely spoil.\n- Product 1 can carry over (6-day shelf life), so a slightly larger buffer is cheap.\n- None of them overflow on the forecast. For example, candidate 0 reaches only about 114 units on day 8.\n\n**Candidate 4 (orders every two days).** It has 13 order days, about 123 more in fees than the three-day plans. In return it puts less pressure on the warehouse limit. Its sizes are reasonable, so it sits just below candidate 5, which may be slightly under-ordered."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5058, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5058}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:00:22.854Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWB7KqNTgayBKsV8Y7GV"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DE3FDUTm7T7mEh8DpCXWF2", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWB7L7EkuWbEADyCBrxx", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DE3FDUTm7T7mEh8DpCXWF2", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.68, 0.3, 0.65, 0.05, 0.42, 0.55, 0.7, 0.2]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": 